{
  "_comment": [
    "Example `<workdir>/crustify/artifacts/schedule.json` of a port campaign, beside the wrap",
    "campaign's in schedule.json, whose comment the fields follow. src/alloc.c is foundational:",
    "its allocator and releaser stay `wrap`, as one policy in one batch. src/core.c is ported,",
    "but widget_handle is `wrap` in its wave 1, since src/io.c's widget_read reads its `flags`:",
    "its `opaque_after` names that user, so its `port/layout` is wave 3, which depends on io.c's",
    "last wave, 2, and runs once io.c is integrated. Its `memory_unmanaged_after` names only",
    "widget_open, a raw site of its own module, so no `port/memory` is planned: the move to",
    "Rust's allocator is part of widget_open's port. widget_open is exported while io.c's C",
    "calls it, and its `port/unexport` shares wave 3; widget_close, which only its own module",
    "calls, has no export and no later stage. Wave 1's batch 3 is core.c's module pass, after",
    "which core.c is integrated, once; its later-stage wave 3 forks from the working branch",
    "after that integration. Wave 2 is running; wave 3's batches are packed when it starts.",
    "An independent illustration: it is not a schedule for templates/modules.json."
  ],
